%N A402825 Number of possible permutations of a Face-Turning Octahedron (FTO) of size n.
%C A402825 A Face-Turning Octahedron (FTO) of size n is a puzzle where the regular octahedron is cut by 4 groups of n-1 equally-spaced planes, the planes in each group being parallel to one of the 4 pairs of opposite faces of the octahedron. In comparison, in the puzzle of a Corner-Turning Octahedron (CTO) the octahedron is cut by 6 groups of n-1 equally-spaced planes not passing through the center, where the planes in each group are perpendicular to one of the 3 lines connecting a pair of opposite vertices of the octahedron; see A309111, A309112.
%H A402825 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402825/b402825.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..16</a>
%H A402825 Puzzling Stack Exchange, <a href="https://puzzling.stackexchange.com/questions/141269/number-of-possible-permutations-of-a-face-turning-octahedron-of-size-n/">Number of possible permutations of a Face-Turning Octahedron of size n</a>.
%H A402825 Chen Shuang, <a href="https://github.com/cs0x7f/cstimer/wiki/Number-of-states-for-twisty-puzzles">Number of states for twisty puzzles</a>, github.
%H A402825 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Face_Turning_Octahedron">Face Turning Octahedron</a>.
%H A402825 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skewb_Diamond">Skewb Diamond</a>.
%F A402825 a(n) = 960 * 144^d * 239500800^(n-2) * 369600^(2*(n^2-3*n+3-d)/3) for n >= 2, where d = 0 if 3 divides n and 1 otherwise. See the Puzzling Stack Exchange link above.
%o A402825 (PARI) a(n) = if(n>1, my(d=(n%3!=0)); 960 * 144^d * 239500800^(n-2) * 369600^(2*(n^2-3*n+3-d)/3), 1)
%Y A402825 Number of possible permutations of: Pyraminx (without tips: A309109, with tips: A309110); Pyramorphix (A330399); Rubik cube (A075152); Face-Turning Octahedron (this sequence); Corner-Turning Octahedron (without tips: A309111, with tips: A309112); Megaminx (A309113).
